# Battle Visual Feedback System

## Battalion Health Display [to-do]
- **[PRIORITY]** Implement health bars in faction colors (blue for user, red for enemy)
- Calculate total battalion health (base_health * quantity)
- Update health visually as damage is taken
- Ensure health depletes proportionally to damage received
- Implement smooth transitions for health changes

## Node Control Visualization [to-do]
- Show node control progress in faction colors (blue for user, red for enemy)
- Display percentage of damage done toward capture threshold (75% of total army health)
- Implement zero-sum visualization where opposing progress first negates existing progress
- Ensure clear transition when node returns to neutral state (0%)
- Animate control state changes for clear visual feedback

## Network Line Effects [to-do]
- When node is captured, connected network lines glow with faction color
- For example: if node 3 is captured, lines to nodes 0, 1, 6, and 7 would glow
- Create subtle pulsing effect to indicate active bonus
- Ensure visual distinction between normal and glowing lines
- Update glow effect immediately when node control changes

## Combat Animation Effects [to-do]
- Create basic attack animations that show direction
- **[LOWER PRIORITY]** Implement damage number popups on hit ("-X" display)
- Ensure animations align with battalion actions
- Add visual indicators for attack range
- Create clear visual feedback for battle events

## Battalion Status Indicators [to-do]
- Display battalion type indicators (Breacher/Guardian/Phreak)
- Show mark level indicators (Mk1-4)
- Implement target indication with visual line to current target
- Create range indicators showing attack area
- Ensure status is clearly visible to players

## Battle Phase Transitions [to-do]
- Create visual countdown for pre-battle phase
- Implement smooth transition to active battle phase
- Design clear battle conclusion visual effects
- Show timer visualization during battle
